Voice-flow patch for the recorded-voice ("dum"/"da") playback engine
=====================================================================

Target: original_base.html (then re-mirror into index.html / "urdu-meter-trainer 2.html"
via scripts/build_app.py, per the project's dual-file convention -- do NOT hand-edit the
mirrors). Matched against the copy of original_base.html read while this patch was written;
each "old" block below is a verbatim, single-occurrence snippet (confirmed via
`grep -Fc` against both original_base.html and index.html: count 1 in each), so it is safe
to apply as a plain text search/replace even if unrelated parts of the file have moved.

This is a pure engine-internals change: no call sites elsewhere in the app (build_app.py's
Studio couplet player, the Ear tab, "Play Rhythm" buttons, etc.) need to change, since they
only ever call play(seq, {feet, cae, onStep, onEnd, ...}) and never touch recSound/
syllableSound/voice/mineSound directly. All new opts fields (footGap, caeGap, xfade) are
optional with defaults, and opts.feet/opts.cae remain optional exactly as before.

Apply as 6 independent find/replace edits, in the style of build_app.py's own
`assert old in html; html = html.replace(old, new)` pattern:

